\pard\qc\b\f0\fs32 Mobility Axiom Manuals V1\par
\pard\qc\b\fs28 Word Format Standard\par
\pard\qc\fs22 Version V1\par
\pard\sa240\par

\pard\b 1. Purpose\par
\pard This standard defines how every Mobility Axiom manual must be created for staff, customers, and internal review.\par
\pard\sa120\par

\pard\b 2. Master Editing Format\par
\pard 1. Primary working format: .docx\par
\pard 2. Word-compatible fallback created by agent: .rtf\par
\pard 3. Delivery format: .pdf exported from Word\par
\pard 4. Markdown may exist only as a backup draft, not as the main personnel working file.\par
\pard\sa120\par

\pard\b 3. Folder Rule\par
\pard All manuals must live under the root folder:\par
\pard\b Mobility Axiom Manuals V1\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard Recommended structure:\par
\pard 1. User\par
\pard 2. Tech\par
\pard 3. Quick Start\par
\pard 4. Shared Assets\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard Language folders must sit inside each manual type, for example:\par
\pard User\EN\par
\pard User\PH\par
\pard User\KR\par
\pard User\TH\par
\pard User\ID\par
\pard User\CN\par
\pard\sa120\par

\pard\b 4. File Naming Rule\par
\pard Use simple professional names:\par
\pard 1. User Manual.docx\par
\pard 2. Technical Manual.docx\par
\pard 3. Quick Start Guide.docx\par
\pard 4. Installation Guide.docx\par
\pard 5. Migration Guide.docx\par
\pard\sa120\par

\pard\b 5. Cover Page Rule\par
\pard Every manual must begin with:\par
\pard 1. Product name\par
\pard 2. Manual title\par
\pard 3. Version\par
\pard 4. Audience\par
\pard 5. Language\par
\pard 6. Date or revision\par
\pard\sa120\par

\pard\b 6. Writing Style Rule\par
\pard 1. Use plain professional English.\par
\pard 2. Use exact UI button and tab names.\par
\pard 3. Use numbered procedures for actions.\par
\pard 4. One action per step.\par
\pard 5. Avoid developer jargon in User manuals.\par
\pard 6. Put technical setup only in Tech manuals.\par
\pard 7. State the expected result after important procedures.\par
\pard 8. Add warnings and notes where the operator can make mistakes.\par
\pard\sa120\par

\pard\b 6.1 First Sign-In Rule (mandatory)\par
\pard Any manual that describes sign-in must include an IMPORTANT — First sign-in subsection when the audience may perform or support a new install. That subsection must cover:\par
\pard 1. One-time default credentials (typically global / global123 on a new server).\par
\pard 2. Forced password change before normal dashboard use.\par
\pard 3. Factory password invalid after change.\par
\pard 4. Step-by-step change-password procedure or cross-reference to it.\par
\pard\sa120\par

\pard\b 7. Required Section Pattern\par
\pard For feature sections in User manuals, use this order:\par
\pard 1. Purpose\par
\pard 2. Before you start (if needed)\par
\pard 3. Step-by-step procedure\par
\pard 4. Expected result\par
\pard 5. Notes\par
\pard 6. Common problems\par
\pard 7. Screenshot placeholder\par
\pard\sa120\par

\pard\b 8. Screenshot Placeholder Rule\par
\pard Use clear placeholders so staff can insert images later.\par
\pard Format example:\par
\pard [Insert Screenshot U-01: Login page with username, password, and language selector]\par
\pard [Insert Diagram T-01: Deployment architecture overview]\par
\pard\sa120\par

\pard\b 9. Word Layout Rule\par
\pard Recommended Word styling:\par
\pard 1. Title: 18 to 20 pt bold\par
\pard 2. Heading 1: 16 pt bold\par
\pard 3. Heading 2: 13 to 14 pt bold\par
\pard 4. Body text: 11 pt\par
\pard 5. Line spacing: 1.15 or 1.2\par
\pard 6. Numbered procedures only for action steps\par
\pard 7. Tables only where they improve clarity\par
\pard\sa120\par

\pard\b 10. Review Rule\par
\pard 1. Operators review User manuals.\par
\pard 2. IT or super admins review Tech manuals.\par
\pard 3. Screenshot insertion happens after wording is stable.\par
\pard 4. PDF export happens only after review pass.\par
\pard\sa120\par

\pard\b 11. Current Standard Decision\par
\pard Mobility Axiom manuals are now Word-first manuals. Future manual work should target Word editing and PDF export, not markdown-only delivery.\par
